{
  "format": "spreadsheet-app",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "GT7 grind comparison",
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "Single Race Payout Comparison",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "About",
          "source": "# Single race payout comparison\n\nThis table shows the expected payout if you were to grind the same race as many times as possible for exactly 8 hours a day, 5 days a week, assuming you don't run a partial race at the end of the day.\n\nFor example, say it consistently takes you 31 minutes to finish Le Mans. After 8 hours with no breaks, you'd have finished Le Mans 15 times with 15 minutes to spare - not enough to finish another race. Thus, the (Le Mans, 31) value only counts the payout for 15 full races. (This is also why the 23 and 24 minute payouts are the same for Tokyo - 70%.)\n\nEach column is your max time plus break time between races, in minutes. A Tokyo row is the share of races you finish with the clean race bonus.\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "name": "Options",
          "rowCount": 1,
          "colCount": 1,
          "cells": [
            {
              "row": 0,
              "col": 0,
              "input": "=CHECKBOX(Config!'Show Spa?'!A1, \"Show Spa\")"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "name": "Payout (8*5 hours)",
          "rowCount": 12,
          "colCount": 22,
          "formats": [
            {
              "startRow": 1,
              "endRow": null,
              "startCol": 1,
              "endCol": null,
              "format": {
                "numberFormat": "#,##0"
              }
            }
          ],
          "conditionalFormats": [
            {
              "startRow": 1,
              "endRow": null,
              "startCol": 1,
              "endCol": null,
              "kind": "scale",
              "low": "red",
              "high": "green"
            }
          ],
          "cells": [
            {
              "row": 0,
              "col": 0,
              "input": "=PayoutByDuration(Config!'Show Spa?'!A1)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "Conclusions",
          "source": "{% let limit = 24 %}\n{% let sardegna = PayoutAt(\"Sardegna\", limit) %}\nIf you can finish Sardegna in {{ limit }} minutes or less, then Tokyo is only better if:\n\n{% for race in RaceNames %}{% if LEFT(race, 5) = \"Tokyo\" %}{% let longest = LongestRunPayingOver(race, sardegna) %}{% if longest > 0 %}\n- You can finish in {{ longest }} minutes or less with the clean race bonus at least {{ VALUE(MID(race, 9, 3)) }}% of the time.{% end %}{% end %}{% end %}\n\nSardegna at {{ limit }} minutes pays **{{ TEXT(sardegna, \"#,##0\") }}** credits over the 40 hours. A Tokyo row that is missing above pays less than that at every time in the table.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
